1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,400
Raw screen recordings feel slow, and the reason is dead air.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,400
Every pause, every moment of thinking, makes the viewer drift away.

3
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:14,400
Pare finds those pauses and cuts them out on exact frame boundaries.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,400
Audio and video stay in sync, even after hundreds of jump cuts.

5
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:24,400
Next it brings the loudness up to the level YouTube expects.

6
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,400
Your subtitles are re-timed, so they still match the edited video.

7
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:34,400
Then they are burned in, clear of the webcam in the corner.

8
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:39,400
An assistant reads the transcript and picks a few punchy highlights.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,400
Those become a short teaser that opens the video.

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:49,400
It also drafts chapter titles you can paste into the description.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,400
Not happy with a choice? Edit the plan file and render again.

12
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:59,400
One command, from a raw recording to something worth watching.
